From 734eb8badc80c621eac59bb496d2e58344ee1d55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Horchynskyi <pan.alexeu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:09:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] deko3d: each shader's prepared info kept in
 cache/info_shaders.bin; first-use reads counted

A pixel shader's first draw converted its whole SPIR-V to GLSL just to learn the interpolators it reads (InfoDe), 5-10 ms
on the ring thread, every session: Singularity's lightning, ~150 shaders drawn for the first time in one frame, froze for
a second. InfoDe's results (SPIR-V fingerprint, specialization mask, interpolators), keyed by the container fingerprint,
are saved in cache/info_shaders.bin and loaded at start; a PC tool can write the file for a whole shader library.
PrimerosUsos tells how many compiled shaders a long frame read from the cache file and how long the first-time work took.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CGstJFihyJYNUGR3QC7gUu
